      "heading": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test",
      "content": {
        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "A mechanical engineer can switch to software testing or other IT roles by building programming and testing basics, showing a project, and using engineering strengths in analysis, documentation and systems thinking, but the move needs steady practice and realistic expectations about entry roles."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Start with testing or support roles where tools are learnable, build a small project and decide later whether to deepen in testing, automation or development."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Course placement claims are often exaggerated."
          }
        ]
      },
